#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:52
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kjumpingcube; is a simple tactical game. You can play it against the "
"computer or against a friend. The playing area consists of squares that "
"contain points. Each square starts with just one point, no owner and a "
"neutral color."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You move by clicking on a neutral square or one you already own. If you "
"click on a neutral square, you gain ownership and it changes to your playing "
"color. Each time you click on a square, the points increase by one. If the "
"square's points reach a maximum, one point will jump to each of the square's "
"neighbors."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a neighboring square is owned by the other player, it gets taken over, "
"together with all of its points, and changes color. For example, if a square "
"in the centre reaches five points, four of its points go to its four "
"neighbors, leaving it with one point. It is possible for a cascade of "
"automatic moves to occur if the neighbors also reach a maximum. Large parts "
"of the playing area can change hands very rapidly."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:72 index.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid "The winner is the player who ends up owning all the squares."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to Play &kjumpingcube;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A move consists of clicking on a square that does not belong to your "
"opponent."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid "The move increases the points in the square by one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At the start of the game, each square has one point, is painted a neutral "
"color and has no owner."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid "Each player has a color to mark ownership of squares."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By clicking a square that has no owner, you become the owner and it changes "
"to your color, as well as adding one point."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a square has more points than it has neighbors, one point jumps to each "
"of the neighbors, leaving one point in the original square."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"During such a move, all the neighboring squares become owned by the player "
"who moved and so do all of their points, even if the neighbors were neutral "
"or owned by the other player before."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Neighbors are the squares above, below, left and right: not diagonally "
"located squares. Corner squares have two neighbors, side squares have three "
"and centre squares have four."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a move leaves a neighbor with a maximum number of points, the move "
"continues automatically to the neighbor's neighbors and so on, in a cascade. "
"A large number of squares can change ownership during such a move."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure "
"&kjumpingcube;</guimenuitem></menuchoice> to select colors, computer player, "
"skill level and board size."
msgstr ""

