#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:320
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tips, Tricks and Hints"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:323
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Try to avoid increasing a square when your opponent owns a neighboring "
"square that can reach its maximum before your square does."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:327
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Try to get control of the corner squares first, then the side squares. You "
"need fewer moves to make them reach a maximum."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:331
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Try not to play too close to your opponent, especially during the opening "
"moves. Drop back a square or two or pick a square on the diagonal from your "
"opponent."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:335
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Keep an eye out for long chains of squares that are almost at their maximum. "
"If they are yours, you must guard them against cascading moves. If they are "
"your opponent's, they can become ripe for capture by a cascading move, just "
"as soon as they extend close enough to your territory."
msgstr ""

